  "term": "SDS",
  "definition": "SDS refers to the Sheehan Disability Scale, a standardized questionnaire used to assess how much symptoms such as panic, anxiety, phobia, or depression interfere with functioning at work or school, in social life, and in family life. It provides separate ratings for these areas and an overall disability score.",
